::Q1::What is prompt engineering?
{
~Training a model from scratch~Installing an operating system
~Managing cloud storage
=Writing model input so it reliably produces useful output
}


::Q2::Why is context useful in a prompt?
{
~It replaces all constraints
~It automatically verifies every answer~It prevents the model from reading the instruction
=It provides relevant background information needed for a useful response
} 


::Q3::What is iterative prompting?
{
=Refining a prompt based on the quality of the response
~Sending one prompt and never reviewing the output
~Training a new model after every response
~Deleting the prompt after it is sent
} 


::Q4::Why does providing examples often improve a prompt?
{
~Examples automatically increase the model's training data
~Examples guarantee the model will never hallucinate
~Examples eliminate the need for an instruction=Examples can demonstrate the desired pattern or format
} 


::Q5::What is a common prompting mistake?
{
~Providing relevant background
~Iterating after reviewing the response~Clearly specifying the desired format
=Giving a vague request without enough context or constraints
}
